Acceptance evidence:
Layout allocates through ui-model::layout::solve_box; host width/origin only. Child DOM bounds and browser font metrics never feed native layout.
Native snapshots reject mismatched child counts. Tests prove flex spacer allocation, baseline alignment, mixed Text runs, reflow after shrinking, wrapping/ellipsis, clamped scroll offset and balanced clipping.
GPU test reads every pixel outside the viewport: scrolling real rows changes only the viewport, and top/end images differ.
Box gallery: 4 materials × 4 densities × 2 themes = 32 images, each with radii 0/6/12/20. Plus 24 scroll and 8 Text images = 64.

Parity: 24/24 over tolerance before -> 24/24 after. No count improvement claimed.
Worst changed fraction: 1.84% -> 1.67%; unchanged channel tolerance 8 and changed-pixel budget 0.1%.
box maximum child geometry error: 0.461620 -> 0.461620 logical px.
text maximum child geometry error: 1.446777 -> 0.014893 logical px.
stack maximum child geometry error: 0.034378 -> 0.025391 logical px.
Web reference PNG bytes identical: 24/24. Geometry improvement did not change the reference.

Residuals at their owning layer:
L1 fractional paint bounds: Card y=65.59375 in both layout trees, native snaps its top paint to row 66 while CSS covers rows 65/66; e.g. x623 row65 web RGB33,36,64, native11,11,16 (background). Do not compensate in L6 geometry.
L1 text-mask/coverage differences remain visible across the type scale. Tracked BAND advance differs by 0.461620 px; untracked Text snapshot max is 0.014893 px.
L6 limits: selection is metadata until the input controller; wrapping is word-based without hyphenation, unbreakable words can overflow. Native draw lists retain rounded clip chains, but material surfaces intersect ancestor clips as rectangles. Opacity/dim use existing per-colour transforms rather than isolated CSS group opacity.
Not checked: Linux text backend, wheel/selection interaction, rounded material/group-opacity CSS parity, full legacy module parity matrix. No FPS measured, no operator browser opened/reloaded.

